@startuml Import chain

!pragma teoz true

title Import chain (gontroller): walk -> group -> gate -> identify -> exif -> commit;\nevery participant is a step (own goroutine), every arrow is a channel (closed when its writers are done)

box "walk: the files" #LightCyan
control "walk\n(the entry)" as Walker
end box

box "group: whole assets (a sub-chain)" #LightCyan
control "switch\n(first that claims)" as Groups
control "Apple Photos\ngrouper" as Photos
control "plain folder\ngrouper (last)" as Generic
end box

box "gate: the files table" #LightGreen
control "gate" as Gate
end box

box "identify: the item known (exiftool lives here)" #Lavender
control "read\n(N in parallel, no DB)" as Exif
control "validate\n(one at a time)" as Validator #LightGreen
control "show\n(cheap preview)" as Preview #LightYellow
end box

box "exif: the EXIF perceptors, their values kept" #Honeydew
control "built in\n(exif_date, exif_size, ...)" as Core
control "external\n(.so)" as Plugins
control "keep\n(the perceptors' values)" as Keep
end box

box "commit: the item published" #MistyRose
control "close" as Closer
end box

box "importer (the top)" #WhiteSmoke
control "the passes,\nRefresh" as Top
end box

database "DB" as DB

== files flow in; groups flow out one by one, steps run concurrently ==

Top -> Walker: a new chain, Process: a pass starts the entry

loop every file under the root
    Walker -> DB: its row: created / stat refreshed,\nCheckTime (Changed: new or stat changed)
    Walker -> Groups: dto.WalkedFile (the row)
    note left of Walker
    Unreadable directory:
    skipped, recorded (V1)
    end note
end

alt Apple claims it (inside *.photoslibrary)
    Groups -> Photos: file
    Photos -> Photos: first file: asset links from Photos.sqlite\n(original, render, Live Photo video); buffer of open\ngroups, a group goes out when all its files arrived
    Photos -> Gate: dto.Asset (asset UUID; a file of an asset\ntrashed / hidden in Photos: in Missing)
else nobody else claims it (other providers: Immich, ... later)
    Groups -> Generic: file
    Generic -> Generic: sidecars by name, next to each other\n(buffer: one open group; a complete group goes out)
    Generic -> Gate: dto.Asset
end
note over Groups: a provider not enabled is not asked:\nits files are a plain folder's

opt the asset's Missing
    Gate -> DB: the model's Gone: a main file's item deleted,\na sidecar's item Dirty
end
alt unchanged, the model says no work (NeedsWork)
    Gate ->x Gate: drop
else changed (stat, a role the grouper gave) / needs work (Rework, ...)
    Gate -> Exif: dto.Asset
end

Exif -> Exif: ONE exiftool -j call for the group (only the declared tags);\nkind of every file (exif MIMEType, own extension table, sniff),\nthe main file first, roles; the metadata package (the source >\n.xmp > main > derivatives; only the perceptors' tags);\nthe main file's fingerprint: size + sha256(first, last 64 KB)
Exif -> Validator: draft (private to identify)

Validator -> DB: not media / broken: ignored; else by path and\nfingerprint: same / changed / moved / duplicate
Validator -> Preview: item (GUID) + draft

Preview -> DB: pixels, codec of every file
Preview -> Preview: what the browser shows now, no transcode:\nShow / the main file (JPEG, PNG, ...; H.264 video) /\nthe biggest viewable derivative / the main file's embedded\npreview (exiftool -b into the cache); any size counts
Preview -> Core: identify.Item (the item + its metadata package;\nthe draft stays in identify)
Core -> Plugins: + date, size, length (written into the item)
Plugins -> Keep: + the external perceptors' values (read-only)
Keep -> DB: a row in every import perceptor's storage
Keep -> Closer: item
Closer -> DB: Visible (a preview) or Waiting (none)
note right of Closer
The client gets Visible (and Ready)
items at once. Ready comes later from
the expensive chain (transcode, fed
from the DB; roadmap: thumbnails)
end note

== end of walk ==

loop every row the walk did not stamp that it says is missing (V2: a complete walk,\nunder the root, not under unreadable directories)
    Walker -> Groups: dto.WalkedFile (Missing): to its provider's grouper,\nwhich passes it through (Asset.Missing) or makes something of it
end
Walker -> Groups: the walk returns: its channel CLOSES
Groups -> Photos: the switch returns: every grouper's input closes
& Groups -> Generic: closed
Generic -> Gate: what it holds (last group); returns
Photos -> Gate: returns (an incomplete group waits for the next walk)
note over Gate: the gate's input closes once every grouper has returned\n(a WaitGroup per channel); so on, step by step, to the end
Closer --> Top: Process returns: every step has;\nevery group of the walk went through every step
Top -> Top: rescan pause (1 min), then the next pass

== One asset again (Apple Photos on demand) ==
note over Photos: Photos made a file of an asset local\n(the viewer asked for it: PhotoKit)
Photos -> Top: Refresh(uuid)
Top -> DB: MarkRework (updated_at untouched: no delta brings\nthe item back); the next pass processes it (NeedsWork)
note over Top: no waiting: the client guesses meanwhile\n(the tile's cloud goes once it got the original)

@enduml
